    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The audit line confirms the new behavior end-to-end:\n\n```\n{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nNote `memberId=NSWV2\u2026` (V2-tagged region inside the identifier) while `ownerSegment=STANDARD_METRO` (METRO still derived from the plain `NSW` region).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (`OwnerDerivations.java`) \u2014 added a fixed `IDENTITY_VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` mixed into every identifier so all values differ from v1 and none recur:\n- `identifierRegion` \u2192 `region(...) + \"V2\"`, so `memberId`'s embedded region (and its Luhn check digit) changes.\n- `identityKey` \u2192 `SHA-256(\"V2|\" + tel + \"|\" + mail + \"|\" + soundex(lastName))`.\n- `householdId` \u2192 `SHA-256(\"V2|\" + lastName + \"|\" + postcode)`.\n- `locality` now derives the plain region straight from the owner's fields (`postcode`/`city`) instead of parsing it back out of the (now-tagged) `memberId`; removed the obsolete `memberIdRegion` helper. `timezone` and the owner-segment area stay on this plain region, so the `V2` tag never leaks into user-facing fields. Updated `Owner.getLocality()` to the new 2-arg signature.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- Added an `OwnerIdentity` schema (`memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey`) and moved those three off the top-level `Owner` into a nested `identity` object.\n- Added a top-level `apiVersion` integer (constant `2` via MapStruct).\n- Mapper builds `identity.*` from the owner and sets `apiVersion`, with matching reverse mappings.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreationAuditor`) \u2014 bumped to schema v2: added `\"schemaVersion\": 2` and the `ownerSegment` recomputed from the v2 identity; the reported `memberId` is now the v2 value automatically.\n\nThe provided `AcceptanceTest` (verifying `$.apiVersion == 2`, the nested `$.identity.*` fields, and absence of the old top-level fields) passes, and the full suite is green.",
