    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, traced from the request boundary through to the response. I've kept it in strict execution order and marked each step as a **validation** (can reject the request) or a **side-effect** (mutates state / the outside world).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **[validation] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner`. The caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected (403) before any logic runs.\n\n2. **[validation] Bean Validation of the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (declared on the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner`). Jakarta constraints on the DTO are checked; any violation yields 400:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (only if present)\n   - `postcode`: `@Size(4..4)` (only if present)\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`: `@Pattern(.*\\S.*)`, `@Size(1..255)` (each only if present)\n\n## In `addOwner` (idempotency gate)\n\n3. **[side-effect / short-circuit] Idempotency-Key replay check** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header is present and non-blank and that key is already recorded in the in-memory `idempotentCreates` map, the previously-created owner is looked up; if it still exists, it is returned with **200 OK** and none of the steps below run (no new owner created).\n\n## In `createNewOwner` \u2014 normalization & field validation (`normalizeNewOwner`)\n\n4. **[side-effect] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** via `ownerMapper.toOwner` (id and pets ignored).\n\n5. **[validation + side-effect] Address normalization** (`normalizeAddressFields`): prefers structured `addressLine1` (+ optional `addressLine2`), else the flat `address`. Each is trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, and common abbreviations expanded (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`); the flat `address` is (re)composed and written back. **Rejects 400** if neither an `addressLine1` nor an `address` remains after normalization.\n\n6. **[validation + side-effect] Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`Telephones.toE164`). The normalized value is written back. **Rejects 400** if it cannot form a valid E.164 number.\n\n7. **[side-effect + validation] Email normalization** \u2014 if an email is present, it is lower-cased and written back, then checked against the disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). **Rejects 400** if the domain is disposable.\n\n8. **[validation] Postcode vs. locality** (`postcodeValidForLocality`). A present postcode must be exactly 4 digits and, where the region has a known range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall within it. **Rejects 400** otherwise. (Absent postcode is accepted.)\n\n9. **[validation + side-effect] Registration date**:\n   - If absent, defaults to today (`LocalDate.now()`).\n   - **Rejects 400** if a supplied date is in the future (after today).\n   - Then rolls forward to the next business day, skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday set, and writes the adjusted date back.\n\n## In `createNewOwner` \u2014 cross-record gates\n\n10. **[validation] Daily creation cap** (`dailyLimitReached`) \u2014 **rejects 429** if 100 or more existing owners already carry this (adjusted) registration date.\n\n11. **[validation] City hard capacity** (`cityIsAtCapacity`) \u2014 **rejects 409** if the owner's city (case-insensitive, trimmed) already holds 50 or more owners.\n\n12. **[side-effect] Assign household id** \u2014 `owner.setHouseholdId(owner.computeHouseholdId())` (derived from normalized last name + postcode).\n\n13. **[validation] Duplicate identity** (`isDuplicateIdentity`) \u2014 **rejects 409** if any active (non-deleted) owner shares this owner's identity key (SHA-256 over `V2 | telephone | email | soundex(lastName)`).\n\n## In `createNewOwner` \u2014 derived attribute assignment (`assignDerivedAttributes`)\n\nHousehold membership is first resolved: `findHouseholdMembers` finds active owners sharing the same last name + postcode; `declaredHouseholdMember` = joins an existing household **and** `sharesHousehold` is true. Then, all as **side-effects** on the owner:\n\n14. **memberId** \u2014 `deduplicatedMemberId`: computes `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and, if it collides with an existing owner's member id, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n15. **namesakeCount** \u2014 count of existing owners sharing the same first + last name (case-insensitive).\n16. **bulkSignupWarning** \u2014 true if more than 80 existing owners share this registration date.\n17. **capacityWarning** \u2014 true if the city currently holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching capacity).\n18. **householdSize** \u2014 existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus this one.\n19. **membershipLevelCap** \u2014 one above the highest membership level held by existing household members, else null.\n20. **possibleDuplicate / possibleDuplicateOf** (`assignPossibleDuplicate`): a declared household member is forced to `false`/null; otherwise flags `true` and records the lowest-id soft-match (same postcode + same last-name Soundex but different identity key), else `false`/null.\n\n## In `createNewOwner` \u2014 commit & outward effects\n\n21. **[side-effect] Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.\n22. **[side-effect] Audit** \u2014 `ownerCreationAuditor.auditOwnerCreated`: emits two lines to the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 a human-readable line and a structured single-line JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event (schemaVersion 2, incrementing `seq`, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment).\n23. **[side-effect] Welcome notification** \u2014 `welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome`: emits a line to the `NOTIFY` logger carrying the owner id and member id.\n24. **[side-effect] Build response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Back in `addOwner` (idempotency record)\n\n25. **[side-effect] Record idempotency mapping** \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied and the response was 201 with a non-null id, `idempotentCreates.putIfAbsent(key, id)` so a later retry with the same key replays step 3.\n\n**Notes on ordering semantics:** validations short-circuit in the sequence above, so the *first* failing gate determines the status returned \u2014 field/normalization failures (400) precede the daily cap (429), which precedes city capacity and identity-duplicate (both 409). The derived-attribute steps (14\u201320) never reject; they only annotate the owner. The three outward effects (persist, audit, notify) happen only after every gate has passed."
